DELETE FROM Product;

insert into Product (product_key) VALUES 
('5'),
('6');


Write a solution to report the customer ids from the Customer table that bought all the products in the Product table.
Return the result table in any order.

My solution :

SELECT customer_id
FROM (
SELECT c.customer_id, count(DISTINCT c.product_key) as calcul, (SELECT COUNT(product_key) FROM Product) as reference
FROM Customer c
LEFT JOIN Product p on c.product_key = p.product_key
GROUP BY c.customer_id) t
WHERE calcul = reference

-- OR --

SELECT  customer_id 
FROM Customer 
GROUP BY customer_id
HAVING COUNT(distinct product_key) = (SELECT COUNT(product_key) FROM Product)
